                <pb facs="0351" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg271"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay directs Mr. Conger to take an early opportunity to advise Prince Ch’ing
                    that the President trusts and expects that no arrangement which will permanently
                    impair the territorial integrity of China, or injure the legitimate interests of
                    the United States, or impair the ability of China to meet her international
                    obligations, will be made with any single power.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
